make visible or obscure."}, {"id": "b6c0a2ef-fd7e-40fa-9c8e-85e88d4b09a4", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Comparative methods", "children": [{"id": "03f6d628-ac5c-4250-bf7b-2fdb884462dc", "type": "concept", "title": "Motifs across traditions"}, {"id": "cf2a1b0e-a881-4a10-9027-a8e79d3ffe7c", "type": "concept", "title": "Genre migration"}, {"id": "68f43e19-be71-401e-a966-e7e4ea51c8b8", "type": "concept", "title": "Influence and adaptation"}, {"id": "cea6e10f-8f84-425a-968e-1743707fc495", "type": "concept", "title": "Reception across borders"}], "description": "Gist: Comparative reading reveals patterns across language, form, period, and culture."}, {"id": "f873617d-4b33-47de-a9c8-5a7b884baade", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Global circulation", "children": [{"id": "18b4dbe9-2f7e-4df8-981a-073f7f37166d", "type": "concept", "title": "World literature debates"}, {"id": "038ff1ca-6de7-4d02-a541-471f745d39d5", "type": "concept", "title": "Diaspora"}, {"id": "2fae6263-f704-45ff-9322-03a870d30ee8", "type": "concept", "title": "Colonial and postcolonial contexts"}, {"id": "d9820ecf-f7b2-4eb9-9b54-e3d777207e06", "type": "concept", "title": "Literary prizes"}], "description": "Gist: Literature travels through empire, migration, diaspora, education, publishing, and media."}]}, {"id": "f5cdd6ca-4fc6-4a93-81cd-a7e1e3d6eb12", "type": "topic", "title": "Canon, Power, Identity, and Representation", "description": "Teach students to ask how literary value, inclusion, exclusion, identity, and power shape reading practices.", "children": [{"id": "4ad63f93-5166-4d7f-9c35-630b5ef4e7a6", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Canon formation", "children": [{"id": "9d8a0e1a-b987-42c6-bfb5-abb4515f7afe", "type": "concept", "title": "Anthologies"}, {"id": "84566766-1b7c-41c5-9e4d-5d7d38a2115e", "type": "concept", "title": "School curricula"}, {"id": "d1da5b2d-ebf8-44f2-9f46-ac6278b50232", "type": "concept", "title": "Prizes"}, {"id": "b7272511-482e-4dd9-ba7f-c5dc9ff01751", "type": "concept", "title": "Recovery work"}], "description": "Gist: Students ask how some texts become central and others become marginal or invisible."}, {"id": "2fdc595f-6d3b-4ae0-87b1-841a4a391fa7", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Identity and representation", "children": [{"id": "caad91ec-d332-4e2a-940a-69f1342f3740", "type": "concept", "title": "Stereotype"}, {"id": "4388514b-8914-4e5d-b22d-575956f32c61", "type": "concept", "title": "Voice"}, {"id": "5f3dccb9-b068-45c8-ada5-e9973b81bb86", "type": "concept", "title": "Point of view"}, {"id": "eb4f4386-b608-42d2-bebb-56307032b21b", "type": "concept", "title": "Self-representation"}], "description": "Gist: Literary texts participate in constructing race, gender, sexuality, class, nation, disability, and religion."}, {"id": "f90232b6-dfac-4039-8d45-954228903cd0", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Ethical reading", "children": [{"id": "048b8551-61ca-4abc-96fa-614321cb5d11", "type": "concept", "title": "Historical humility"}, {"id": "4ce9caa4-8fc6-45b0-9b62-5bf1f253971b", "type": "concept", "title": "Avoiding presentism"}, {"id": "e835c623-8c49-4854-b5e9-f24b98a55cb5", "type": "concept", "title": "Respectful terminology"}, {"id": "56855544-d71b-4bb5-aaeb-2f179e394ce8", "type": "concept", "title": "Accountable claims"}], "description": "Gist: Interpretation carries responsibilities toward authors, contexts, communities, and evidence."}]}, {"id": "1c81c512-6007-464f-9e0f-5d72c966cc20", "type": "topic", "title": "Secondary Sources and Literary Research", "description": "Help students enter scholarly conversations through databases, sources, annotations, and research questions.", "children": [{"id": "7069be11-555b-46fc-8a94-60e962e51006", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Finding scholarship", "children": [{"id": "b6b1958a-4ba2-48c1-9284-af95b9274694", "type": "concept", "title": "MLA International Bibliography"}, {"id": "b50712f9-f9f9-485a-a7a9-40d5f6bf6ddd", "type": "concept", "title": "JSTOR"}, {"id": "3322c8ea-0b8e-4ecb-8b1d-a7f1d0d48a33", "type": "concept", "title": "Project MUSE"}, {"id": "037efbf0-a0be-4f65-b629-4ef60a0da513", "type": "concept", "title": "Library catalogs"}], "description": "Gist: Students learn how literary research begins with databases, bibliographies, and good search terms."}, {"id": "dce6f8dd-1ccd-4f31-88a9-7f00a4c9e48b", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Using secondary sources", "children": [{"id": "d80f74bc-fd6b-4d7b-ae53-607596f509c0", "type": "concept", "title": "Summary"}, {"id": "ce00edce-cb21-49ba-a9be-f2511d253ccb", "type": "concept", "title": "Quotation"}, {"id": "fb84d346-614f-453b-97f9-9ea4ee5dbbf8", "type": "concept", "title": "Synthesis"}, {"id": "4d95eba2-2e40-47a9-889b-71ba98b7146f", "type": "concept", "title": "Source conversation"}], "description": "Gist: Scholarly sources should sharpen, complicate, or challenge a student's own reading."}, {"id": "7ecbcf4f-b22f-4fba-aac6-c0af5e741518", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Research questions", "children": [{"id": "8d2be408-29ba-4e6b-8363-46b32cbe4938", "type": "concept", "title": "Scope"}, {"id": "5e1ef148-30e1-45ff-9e24-c48792a0fa82", "type": "concept", "title": "Significance"}, {"id": "0d2e870b-9bd4-4762-b492-997cce57ed7e", "type": "concept", "title": "Feasibility"}, {"id": "7e1dd650-6ba4-4c36-b59c-3872725171fa", "type": "concept", "title": "Scholarly stakes"}], "description": "Gist: A strong research question turns curiosity into a focused project."}]}, {"id": "14ef0105-4c55-46ba-9e63-072b54cecb32", "type": "topic", "title": "Writing Literary Analysis Essays", "description": "Develop arguable, evidence-based literary essays through thesis, close reading, structure, and revision.", "children": [{"id": "c6adcebb-5a01-424d-8800-59177e99450f", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Thesis and argument", "children": [{"id": "365b8b03-569e-4047-a46d-8b1e5443baec", "type": "concept", "title": "Specific thesis"}, {"id": "49111f83-fd1a-4c58-8cbf-f8c3f7195b28", "type": "concept", "title": "Stakes"}, {"id": "c5fdecc8-2037-4b2f-89f6-6eb4e34af52f", "type": "concept", "title": "Evidence map"}, {"id": "e10fa550-4d9f-486d-b843-5274dd52e920", "type": "concept", "title": "Counter-reading"}], "description": "Gist: Literary essays need arguable claims about how and why a text means."}, {"id": "ebc64cc5-bdf2-4651-b3b7-874e736c1c5f", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Evidence and close reading", "children": [{"id": "eca3085e-6c32-441f-bbc1-51bc340bc074", "type": "concept", "title": "Signal phrases"}, {"id": "2e13a199-9d81-41ef-8095-8e01755cbc3c", "type": "concept", "title": "Quotation integration"}, {"id": "edba243e-07dd-4d97-b425-f74aa1190de4", "type": "concept", "title": "Line-level analysis"}, {"id": "7ef002cb-3a36-4b28-89ed-262ef72c4be6", "type": "concept", "title": "Commentary"}], "description": "Gist: Quotations must be framed, analyzed, and tied back to the argument."}, {"id": "788a5272-9010-4dca-9e97-241abba1ec58", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Essay structure and revision", "children": [{"id": "0230442f-864d-408c-9057-c8c54295b3a7", "type": "concept", "title": "Introductions"}, {"id": "5cdd76bb-6cbc-49d8-a3f9-efdf844049a6", "type": "concept", "title": "Paragraph movement"}, {"id": "7becd7ec-7502-4eb4-8203-76a61a4c5a85", "type": "concept", "title": "Transitions"}, {"id": "93090e63-9927-4633-b39d-6d7e53d9bce2", "type": "concept", "title": "Global revision"}], "description": "Gist: Students learn to build essays that develop rather than repeat a claim."}]}, {"id": "b642e596-a046-46b2-b9fc-99f06196f88c", "type": "topic", "title": "MLA Citation, Academic Integrity, and Scholarly Practice", "description": "Build responsible documentation habits and ethical participation in academic literary study.", "children": [{"id": "37dda7a8-8a5d-4500-ab62-2a73dc754db9", "type": "subtopic", "title": "MLA style", "children": [{"id": "1ae71d9f-b7f2-4c0c-b8af-be8804bfce97", "type": "concept", "title": "In-text citations"}, {"id": "fae378fd-c052-412e-b6ca-5b2ef13da116", "type": "concept", "title": "Works Cited"}, {"id": "c5ee0d1c-d6bc-4008-b6ea-a5070a743db3", "type": "concept", "title": "Poetry and drama citation"}, {"id": "dbf62bc0-d0c7-4a14-969b-c16b23abadbe", "type": "concept", "title": "Editions and translations"}], "description": "Gist: MLA documentation teaches students how literary scholars cite texts and sources."}, {"id": "34ba2890-ffe0-4ee7-87b1-ca6d79fd58dd", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Academic integrity", "children": [{"id": "bff0d2fc-ec59-4c65-bbe3-f6e7eab86455", "type": "concept", "title": "Attribution"}, {"id": "cff445af-17a0-440e-9b05-93f02b7742e8", "type": "concept", "title": "Paraphrase"}, {"id": "14d0c687-49c9-4a19-86de-aaa0dd4b2f59", "type": "concept", "title": "Common knowledge"}, {"id": "620fb147-a08e-4fd2-af4f-fc0660feeb75", "type": "concept", "title": "AI and writing transparency"}], "description": "Gist: Integrity is more than avoiding plagiarism; it is fair representation of sources and labor."}, {"id": "3add583f-6494-41ae-8385-469c07de5d66", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Scholarly professionalism", "children": [{"id": "75c1525f-fb5c-4ca3-a01c-44f7cc380edc", "type": "concept", "title": "Formatting"}, {"id": "9d5d1d0b-1c29-4033-86a5-b8f3b80790a5", "type": "concept", "title": "Revision records"}, {"id": "1ddda86c-4dea-421e-b027-a28a6ddc526e", "type": "concept", "title": "Peer review etiquette"}, {"id": "22f28ca5-bd26-4798-b0c4-f8b3e09ec007", "type": "concept", "title": "Submission standards"}], "description": "Gist: Students practice habits that make their work legible to academic readers."}]}, {"id": "d614b24e-e605-4c84-877b-d49aa2ed00c0", "type": "topic", "title": "Capstone: Close Reading Portfolio and Critical Essay", "description": "Synthesize reading, research, argument, revision, citation, and reflection in a polished introductory portfolio.", "children": [{"id": "dd152a0c-0793-4233-940b-e259dc31cab7", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Portfolio selection", "children": [{"id": "596e1569-bf7e-40b8-922c-1ca4d2585219", "type": "concept", "title": "Annotations"}, {"id": "0b4d